 "kind": "industrial",
 "question": "An engineering school must schedule 8 exams: Statistics, Machine Learning, Operations Research, Logistics, Cost Evaluation, Lean Management, Cryptography, Control Systems. Two exams that share at least one student cannot take place in the same time slot. These pairs share students: Statistics and Machine Learning; Statistics and Operations Research; Statistics and Logistics; Machine Learning and Operations Research; Machine Learning and Cryptography; Machine Learning and Control Systems; Operations Research and Logistics; Operations Research and Cost Evaluation; Logistics and Lean Management; Cost Evaluation and Lean Management; Cost Evaluation and Control Systems; Lean Management and Control Systems; Cryptography and Control Systems; Statistics and Control Systems. What is the minimum number of time slots needed so that no student has two exams at the same time?",
